From bafaefd434ad00bca9f03d109afdebdeff1fa881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 03:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix: OL projection from projected starters, OL card bars,
 consistency grade, owner pills everywhere
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OL projection (QB OL tab, RB rushing fan, team Advanced chip, league OL table)
- _olLineByTeamSeason returns an all-null (truthy) slot map for the projection
  season before ESPN answers, so the baseline fallback never fired and every
  team sat at replacement-level talent: the "projected" rank was a monotonic
  transform of last season's rank (LAC #32 because 2025 was #32). Test for
  real starters, count teams whose projection-season line resolved, and keep
  baseline ranks until >=28 of 32 are known (ranksStable was dead code: n is
  always 32).
- The RB fan printed the BASELINE run rank next to the projected score. It now
  shows the projected rank with the baseline in the caption.
- The 20% prior-season anchor is scaled by continuity (share of projected
  starters who were on last year's snap-leader line), so a rebuilt or finally
  healthy line is judged on its starters. With live depth charts LAC projects
  ~#19 in pass protection instead of #32.
- ESPN roster-but-no-depth-chart → talent-first roster fallback instead of last
  season's snap leaders (the backups, for an injury-wrecked line).
- Open cards re-render once league coverage becomes stable, not only when their
  own team's chart lands; a caption says when ranks are still last season's.
- _olProjectedTeamNext is memoised on what can change it.

OL player card
- Market / Snaps / Draft bars collapsed into the 44px label column because the
  note-tag wrapper became the grid's only child (since e7429f0). display:contents
  on the wrapper restores the row (also the trend header and mini-grid).

Consistency grade
- Scored in fixed full PPR so the PPR benchmarks mean the same in every league
  (half-PPR/standard leagues were graded against a bar one format higher).
- Games under 10 offensive snaps (injury exits, kneel-downs) are excluded.
- Non-played weeks were labelled BYE; a real bye is absent from Sleeper's
  payload, so those are inactive/injured weeks and now read DNP.
- Per-game points include the TE premium, completions and attempts like calcFpts.

Owner pills
- Manager-handle pill next to every name in the passing / receiving / rushing
  projection rows, an OWNER column in the rankings table (cache key follows the
  snapshot), and a search row laid out avatar · pos · name/team · pill.
- Chip is a span[role=button]: a nested <button> was being ejected out of the
  search row by the HTML parser.

Tests: test_ol_projection, test_consistency, test_owner_surfaces.
